  "question": {
    ":question/id": "023abbe6-89fe-544d-a3c4-2ee5851ce1a6",
    ":question/problem": "$\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=$\n\n| {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |\n| {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |\n| {{field-10}} | {{field-11}} | {{field-12}} |",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10\\cdot 5 & 10\\cdot (-2) & 10\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot 5 & (-8)\\cdot (-2) & (-8)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 6\\cdot 5 & 6\\cdot (-2) & 6\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 5 & (-2)\\cdot (-2) & (-2)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}50 & -20 & 20 \\\\ -40 & 16 & -16 \\\\ 30 & -12 & 12 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
